  "question": {
    "text": "<math><mn>108&#160;</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of silver (molar mass <math><mn>108&#160;</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> ) is deposited at cathode from <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> solution by a certain quantity of electricity. The volume (in <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> ) of oxygen gas produced at <math><mn>273&#160;</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> and <math><mn>1</mn></math> bar pressure from water by the same quantity of electricity is ________",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5.66",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>108</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>108</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1&#160;</mn><mi></mi><mi>m</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>e</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ag</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#10230;</mo><mi>Ag</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> charge is required to deposit <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mole</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ag</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>O</mi></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#10230;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math><br /><math><mn>2</mn><mi></mi><mi>F</mi></math> charge is required to deposit <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi></mi><mi>m</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>e</mi></math><br /><math><mn>1</mn><mi>F</mi></math> charge will deposit <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>m</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>e</mi></math>&nbsp;of <math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>O</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math>&nbsp; gas.<br /><math><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>n</mn><mi></mi><mi>R</mi><mi></mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.0821</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>273</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>22.4</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5.6&#160;</mn><mi>L</mi></math></p><p>Faraday&#39;s second law of electrolysis states that, when the same quantity of electricity is passed through several electrolytes, the mass of the substances deposited are proportional to their respective equivalent weight.</p>",
